NAT

NAT (Network Address Translation) translates between private and public IP addressing, commonly allowing devices using private addresses to communicate through a public IP.

Example
Private IP
    ↓
   NAT
    ↓
Public IP
    ↓
Internet
🔒 Private IP vs Public IP
Private IP

A private IP address is used inside a private/local network and is not directly routable across the public Internet.

Public IP

A public IP address is Internet-routable and is typically assigned by an ISP or network provider.

Comparison
Private IP	Public IP
Used inside private networks	Used for Internet communication
Not directly Internet-routable	Internet-routable
Commonly used by internal devices	Typically assigned by ISP/provider
📐 Subnet Mask

A subnet mask is used with an IP address to determine which portion represents the network and which portion represents the host.

Example
IP Address:     192.168.1.25
Subnet Mask:    255.255.255.0

Network:        192.168.1.0
Host:           25
Memory
Subnet Mask
↓
Network Portion + Host Portion


12. Network Troubleshooting

A structured troubleshooting approach is more important than simply memorizing commands.

Windows Network Configuration
ipconfig /all

This can display:

IPv4 address
Subnet mask
Default gateway
DNS servers
DHCP information
Network adapter information
13. Linux Network Configuration
IP Address
ip addr
Routing Information
ip route

These commands help identify the device's addressing and routing configuration.

14. Ping Testing
Test Default Gateway
ping <default-gateway>

Purpose:

Tests connectivity between the local computer and its default gateway.

Test External IP Connectivity
ping 8.8.8.8

Purpose:

Tests basic IP connectivity to an external IP address.

This test does not primarily test DNS.

Test DNS Name Resolution
ping google.com

If:

ping 8.8.8.8

works but:

ping google.com

fails, DNS resolution becomes a strong area to investigate.

15. NSLookup
nslookup google.com

nslookup is used to query DNS and troubleshoot name resolution.

Example troubleshooting logic
ping 8.8.8.8 → Works
        ↓
ping google.com → Fails
        ↓
Investigate DNS
        ↓
nslookup google.com
16. Tracert / Traceroute
Windows
tracert google.com
Linux
traceroute google.com

These commands help identify the network path and intermediate hops between the local system and a destination.

